1961 ( [LINK: (MCMLXI) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_numerals] ) was a  [LINK: (common year starting on Sunday) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_year_starting_on_Sunday]  of the  [LINK: (Gregorian calendar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_calendar] , the 1961st year of the  [LINK: (Common Era) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Era]  (CE) and  [LINK: (Anno Domini) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anno_Domini]  (AD) designations, the 961st  year of the  [LINK: (2nd millennium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2nd_millennium] , the 61st  year of the  [LINK: (20th century) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/20th_century] , and the  2nd   year of the  [LINK: (1960s) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1960s]  decade.


# EVENTS #

[LINK: (January 1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_1]  –  [LINK: (Monetary reform in the Soviet Union) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monetary_reform_in_the_Soviet_Union,_1961] .

[LINK: (January 3) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_3] 
United States President  [LINK: (Dwight D. Eisenhower) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dwight_D._Eisenhower]  announces that the United States has severed diplomatic and consular relations with  [LINK: (Cuba) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba]  [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961#cite_note-1]  ( [LINK: (Cuba–United States relations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba%E2%80%93United_States_relations]  are restored in  [LINK: (2015) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2015] ).
 [LINK: (Aero Flight 311) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aero_Flight_311]  (Koivulahti air disaster):  [LINK: (Douglas DC-3) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_DC-3] C OH-LCC of Finnish airline  [LINK: (Aero) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnair]  crashes near  [LINK: (Kvevlax) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kvevlax]  (Koivulahti), on approach to  [LINK: (Vaasa Airport) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaasa_Airport]  in Finland, killing all 25 on board, due to  [LINK: (pilot error) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilot_error] : an investigation finds that the  [LINK: (captain) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_(civil_aviation)]  and  [LINK: (first officer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_officer_(civil_aviation)]  were both exhausted for lack of sleep, and had consumed excessive amounts of alcohol at the time of the crash.

United States President  [LINK: (Dwight D. Eisenhower) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dwight_D._Eisenhower]  announces that the United States has severed diplomatic and consular relations with  [LINK: (Cuba) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba]  [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961#cite_note-1]  ( [LINK: (Cuba–United States relations) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba%E2%80%93United_States_relations]  are restored in  [LINK: (2015) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2015] ).

[LINK: (Aero Flight 311) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aero_Flight_311]  (Koivulahti air disaster):  [LINK: (Douglas DC-3) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_DC-3] C OH-LCC of Finnish airline  [LINK: (Aero) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnair]  crashes near  [LINK: (Kvevlax) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kvevlax]  (Koivulahti), on approach to  [LINK: (Vaasa Airport) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaasa_Airport]  in Finland, killing all 25 on board, due to  [LINK: (pilot error) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilot_error] : an investigation finds that the  [LINK: (captain) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_(civil_aviation)]  and  [LINK: (first officer) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_officer_(civil_aviation)]  were both exhausted for lack of sleep, and had consumed excessive amounts of alcohol at the time of the crash.

[LINK: (January 5) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_5] 
Italian sculptor  [LINK: (Alfredo Fioravanti) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfredo_Fioravanti]  enters the U.S. Consulate in Rome, and confesses that he was part of the team that forged the  [LINK: (Etruscan terracotta warriors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etruscan_terracotta_warriors]  in the  [LINK: (Metropolitan Museum of Art) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art] .
After the  [LINK: (1960 military coup) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1960_Turkish_coup_d%27%C3%A9tat] , General  [LINK: (Cemal Gürsel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cemal_G%C3%BCrsel]  forms the new government of  [LINK: (Turkey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkey]  (25th government).

Italian sculptor  [LINK: (Alfredo Fioravanti) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfredo_Fioravanti]  enters the U.S. Consulate in Rome, and confesses that he was part of the team that forged the  [LINK: (Etruscan terracotta warriors) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etruscan_terracotta_warriors]  in the  [LINK: (Metropolitan Museum of Art) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art] .

After the  [LINK: (1960 military coup) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1960_Turkish_coup_d%27%C3%A9tat] , General  [LINK: (Cemal Gürsel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cemal_G%C3%BCrsel]  forms the new government of  [LINK: (Turkey) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkey]  (25th government).

[LINK: (January 7) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_7]  – Following a four-day conference in  [LINK: (Casablanca) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casablanca] , five African chiefs of state announce plans for a  [LINK: (NATO) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NATO] -type African organization to ensure common defense. The Charter of Casablanca involves the  [LINK: (Casablanca Group) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casablanca_Group] :  [LINK: (Morocco) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morocco] , the  [LINK: (United Arab Republic) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Arab_Republic] ,  [LINK: (Ghana) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghana] ,  [LINK: (Guinea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guinea] , and  [LINK: (Mali) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mali] .

[LINK: (January 8) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_8]  – In France, a  [LINK: (referendum) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_referendum_on_Algerian_self-determination,_1961]  supports  [LINK: (Charles de Gaulle) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_de_Gaulle] 's policies on independence for  [LINK: (Algeria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algeria] .

[LINK: (January 9) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_9]  – British authorities announce they have uncovered a large  [LINK: (Soviet) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_Union]   [LINK: (spy ring) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espionage] , the  [LINK: (Portland spy ring) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portland_spy_ring] , in London.

[LINK: (January 17) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_17] 
President  [LINK: (Dwight Eisenhower) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dwight_Eisenhower]  gives his final  [LINK: (State of the Union Address) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_of_the_Union_Address]  to Congress. In a Farewell Address the same day, he warns of the increasing power of a " [LINK: (military–industrial complex) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military%E2%80%93industrial_complex] ."
 [LINK: (Patrice Lumumba) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrice_Lumumba]  of the  [LINK: (Republic of Congo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republic_of_Congo]  is assassinated. [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961#cite_note-2]

President  [LINK: (Dwight Eisenhower) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dwight_Eisenhower]  gives his final  [LINK: (State of the Union Address) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_of_the_Union_Address]  to Congress. In a Farewell Address the same day, he warns of the increasing power of a " [LINK: (military–industrial complex) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military%E2%80%93industrial_complex] ."

[LINK: (Patrice Lumumba) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrice_Lumumba]  of the  [LINK: (Republic of Congo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republic_of_Congo]  is assassinated. [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961#cite_note-2]

[LINK: (January 23) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_23]  –  [LINK: (Congress of Venezuela) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Congress_of_Venezuela]  adopts a  [LINK: (new constitution) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_Venezuela_(1961)]  (in force until 1999).

[LINK: (January 24) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_24]  –  [LINK: (1961 Goldsboro B-52 crash) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961_Goldsboro_B-52_crash] : A  [LINK: (B-52 Stratofortress) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B-52_Stratofortress] , carrying two  [LINK: (nuclear bombs) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_bomb] , crashes near  [LINK: (Goldsboro, North Carolina) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldsboro,_North_Carolina] .

[LINK: (January 25) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_25] 
In Washington, D.C., President  [LINK: (John F. Kennedy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_F._Kennedy]  delivers the first live presidential  [LINK: (news conference) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/News_conference] . In it, he announces that the  [LINK: (Soviet Union) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_Union]  has freed the two surviving crewmen from the July 1  [LINK: (1960 RB-47 shootdown incident) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1960_RB-47_shootdown_incident]  involving a  [LINK: (USAF) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USAF]  reconnaissance aircraft and a MiG-19 over the  [LINK: (Barents Sea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barents_Sea] .
Acting to halt 'leftist excesses', a  [LINK: (junta) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_dictatorship]  composed of two army officers and four civilians takes over  [LINK: (El Salvador) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Salvador] , ousting another junta that had ruled for three months.

In Washington, D.C., President  [LINK: (John F. Kennedy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_F._Kennedy]  delivers the first live presidential  [LINK: (news conference) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/News_conference] . In it, he announces that the  [LINK: (Soviet Union) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_Union]  has freed the two surviving crewmen from the July 1  [LINK: (1960 RB-47 shootdown incident) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1960_RB-47_shootdown_incident]  involving a  [LINK: (USAF) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USAF]  reconnaissance aircraft and a MiG-19 over the  [LINK: (Barents Sea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barents_Sea] .

Acting to halt 'leftist excesses', a  [LINK: (junta) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_dictatorship]  composed of two army officers and four civilians takes over  [LINK: (El Salvador) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Salvador] , ousting another junta that had ruled for three months.

[LINK: (January 27) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_27]  –  [LINK: (Soviet submarine S-80) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_submarine_S-80]  sinks in the  [LINK: (Barents Sea) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barents_Sea] , killing all 68 crew.

[LINK: (January 28) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_28]  –  [LINK: (Supercar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supercar_(TV_series)] , the first family sci-fi TV series filmed in  [LINK: (Supermarionation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supermarionation] , debuts on  [LINK: (ATV) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Associated_Television]  in the UK.

[LINK: (January 30) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_30]  – President  [LINK: (John F. Kennedy) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_F._Kennedy]  delivers his first  [LINK: (State of the Union Address) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_of_the_Union_Address] . [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961#cite_note-3]

[LINK: (January 31) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_31]  –  [LINK: (Ham) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ham_(chimpanzee)] , a 37-pound (17-kg) male chimpanzee, is rocketed into space aboard  [LINK: (Mercury-Redstone 2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercury-Redstone_2] , in a test of the  [LINK: (Project Mercury) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Mercury]  spacecraft, designed to carry United States  [LINK: (astronauts) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronaut]  into space.

[LINK: (February 1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_1]  – The United States tests its first  [LINK: (Minuteman I) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minuteman_I]  intercontinental ballistic missile. [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961#cite_note-4]

[LINK: (February 4) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_4]  – The  [LINK: (Portuguese Colonial War) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portuguese_Colonial_War]  begins in  [LINK: (Angola) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angola] .

[LINK: (February 5) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_5] – [LINK: (9) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_9]  – In  [LINK: (Congo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republic_of_the_Congo_(L%C3%A9opoldville)] , President  [LINK: (Joseph Kasa-Vubu) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Kasa-Vubu]  names  [LINK: (Joseph Iléo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Il%C3%A9o]  as the new Prime Minister.

[LINK: (February 12) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_12]  – The  [LINK: (USSR) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USSR]  launches  [LINK: (Venera 1) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venera_1]  towards  [LINK: (Venus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus] .

[LINK: (February 13) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_13]  – The  [LINK: (Congo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republic_of_the_Congo_(L%C3%A9opoldville)]  government announces that villagers have killed  [LINK: (Patrice Lumumba) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrice_Lumumba] . [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1961#cite_note-5]

[LINK: (February 14) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_14]  –  [LINK: (Discovery of the chemical elements) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discovery_of_the_chemical_elements] : Element 103,  [LINK: (Lawrencium) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawrencium] , is first synthesized in  [LINK: (Berkeley, California) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkeley,_California] .

[LINK: (February 15) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_15] 
